Problem
- The native macOS CI app made the embedded WebDriver healthy, then disappeared before POST /session.
- The WebDriver service removes its early-exit listener after readiness, so the previous bounded collector could not distinguish a native signal, an exit code, or a Tauri lifecycle return.

Objective
- Attribute the real macOS failure without exposing raw stderr, paths, PIDs, ports, environment variables, or user data.
- Keep production behavior and Windows/Linux E2E launch paths unchanged.

Decisions and reasons
- On macOS E2E only, WebDriver launches a Node observer which spawns the exact bundle executable with shell=false and an empty argument list.
- The observer validates one absolute normalized path, uses fixed bounded signal sets, forwards termination signals, and emits only allowlisted exit categories.
- Fixed E2E lifecycle markers identify main entry, native preparation, setup entry/completion, and event-loop entry/return.
- The diagnostic collector remains bounded by files, directory entries, bytes, lines, and now 16 fixed categories; arbitrary lines are never relayed.
- The stream generation counter moved to its owning module solely to keep lib.rs below the project 230-line ceiling; behavior and memory ordering are unchanged.

